// A `#test_main` fn is given all of `ctxc test`'s arguments after PATH. Its tests have
// none until it hands them theirs, those after the first `--`, with test::pass_args.
//# $ ctxc test . -q one -- a --b
//# exit: 0
//# stdout:
//| the runner has `-q`
//| the runner has `one`
//| the runner has `--`
//| the runner has `a`
//| the runner has `--b`
//| its own: `-q`
//| its own: `one`
//| before test::pass_args: 1 failed
//| one has `a`
//| one has `--b`
//# stderr:
//| ./t.ctx:4: fail: one: test::args{ &t }.len == 2: 0 == 2
